1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,700
<i>I'm looking for a crime boss
from Korea.</i>

2
00:00:02,833 --> 00:00:05,133
<i>Well, I wanted to meet you,
but this will do.</i>

3
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:06,800
<i>She's hiding here
in the Philippines.</i>

4
00:00:06,933 --> 00:00:09,300
<i>She changed her name,
even her face.</i>

5
00:00:09,433 --> 00:00:12,100
<i>Joey, she's not answering
my calls.</i>

6
00:00:12,233 --> 00:00:13,667
<i> Maybe the kid's just busy.</i>

7
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,367
<i> I'm also nervous.</i>

8
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,733
<i>Who are you really,
and why do you keep showing up?</i>

9
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:18,800
<i> How did you meet him?</i>

10
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:20,033
<i> He's my stalker!</i>

11
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:21,567
<i> I saved your life twice.</i>

12
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,667
<i> So my name is Lee Jin Ho.</i>

13
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,333
<i>I'm from the National
Intelligence Service in Korea.</i>

14
00:00:26,467 --> 00:00:27,433
<i> Why are you following me?</i>

15
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:28,933
<i> The woman in the video,</i>

16
00:00:29,067 --> 00:00:31,000
<i>the one you posted on the
internet.</i>

17
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:32,367
<i> That's what I'm looking for.</i>

18
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,933
<i> My problem now is Jin Ho!</i>

19
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,600
<i> He recognized me! He saw me!</i>

20
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:39,367
<i> You're not going anywhere.</i>

21
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:40,867
<i> Let's listen to him first.</i>

22
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,767
<i>What if this is connected
to your father's case?</i>

23
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:44,933
<i> Give me your cell phones.</i>

24
00:00:45,067 --> 00:00:45,867
<i> Your gun.</i>

25
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,867
<i>I really don't trust
that Andrew.</i>

26
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,867
<i>I don't think he sleeps
at someone's house, right?</i>

27
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,233
<i>I knew it, you're really lying
about trusting Jin Ho.</i>

28
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:56,300
<i> Step away from my things.</i>

29
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:58,333
<i> Keep her out of this.</i>

30
00:00:58,467 --> 00:01:00,733
<i> This is between you and me.</i>

31
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,033
Can you stop?

32
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:24,167
Joey?

33
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:28,533
Joey!

34
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:32,333
If you want to kill each other,

35
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:35,000
don't involve other people,
okay?

36
00:01:35,133 --> 00:01:37,667
Jin Ho, what are you doing?
Why are you doing this?

37
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:41,200
Joey, are you okay?
What's this? Hey!

38
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:47,100
He started first.

39
00:01:50,467 --> 00:01:52,167
Why were you looking
at my stuff?

40
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,400
To make sure you are legit.

41
00:01:54,533 --> 00:01:55,900
We can't just trust you.

42
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:57,333
Then you could've asked!

43
00:01:57,467 --> 00:01:59,433
You didn't have to go
through my bag.

44
00:01:59,567 --> 00:02:03,200
Again, I don't trust you.

45
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:04,967
I need proof for myself.

46
00:02:06,133 --> 00:02:09,567
If there's anyone who shouldn't
be trusted here,

47
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,533
it's you because you
just used us.

48
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,067
What?

49
00:02:15,233 --> 00:02:19,167
Yes, I know that's why you
want us to stay,

50
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:22,133
because you want to put this
story on your vlog.

51
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:24,733
You don't care if we get in
danger

52
00:02:24,867 --> 00:02:27,000
as long as you have a story
to tell, right?

53
00:02:28,233 --> 00:02:29,967
You're already caught, Boy.

54
00:02:31,733 --> 00:02:33,433
That's where you're good at.

55
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:35,333
What? You can't say anything,
can you?

56
00:02:35,467 --> 00:02:37,200
Because it's true.

57
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:40,067
You're good at getting other
people into trouble.

58
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,167
Isn't that what you did
to my father?

59
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:43,933
And now, what are you going
to do to us?

60
00:02:44,067 --> 00:02:46,767
Can someone tell me
what's going on right now?

61
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,000
It's like this.

62
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:48,933
She...

63
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:51,000
He...

64
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,467
Joey hates Andrew.

65
00:02:56,367 --> 00:02:59,167
You don't have to explain
to them.

66
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:02,533
Jin Ho, thank you for saving
my life twice,

67
00:03:02,667 --> 00:03:04,900
but you don't have to worry
about me anymore.

68
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,367
Let's go.

69
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,333
Nothing yet?

70
00:03:25,467 --> 00:03:26,533
Nothing.

71
00:03:26,667 --> 00:03:28,367
I've been trying to book
for a while now.

72
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:32,400
But just be steady.
Someone will accept it too.

73
00:03:32,533 --> 00:03:35,400
It's a good thing the Korean
gave us our cellphone back.

74
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:37,933
He should be.

75
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:40,767
Don't he dare not to or else
he'll really get it from me.

76
00:03:47,567 --> 00:03:49,767
Aren't you tired yet?

77
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,033
You see, it's already morning.

78
00:03:52,167 --> 00:03:54,167
Can you please stop including
this in the days

79
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:55,667
you're going to ruin?

80
00:03:56,867 --> 00:03:59,500
Okay, okay. I might be wrong,

81
00:04:00,867 --> 00:04:01,833
but there's a reason.

82
00:04:01,967 --> 00:04:04,367
I don't need your explanation.

83
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,933
You know what I need?

84
00:04:06,067 --> 00:04:07,267
I need you to stay away
from me

85
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,000
because I don't want
to see you again!

86
00:04:12,333 --> 00:04:13,467
Driver!

87
00:04:15,933 --> 00:04:17,033
Let's go, Joey.

88
00:04:19,333 --> 00:04:20,933
Boss Budol, what now?

89
00:04:22,067 --> 00:04:23,533
Let's go on our own ways.

90
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:28,667
Driver...

91
00:04:44,967 --> 00:04:47,267
This is not over yet, Joey.

92
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,233
What, let's go?

93
00:05:05,367 --> 00:05:07,233
We're just being suspicious.

94
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:11,967
No one's following us, right?

95
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:13,100
It's quiet.

96
00:05:13,233 --> 00:05:14,433
No one's around.

97
00:05:14,567 --> 00:05:19,300
So that means those who followed
us don't know where we live.

98
00:05:19,433 --> 00:05:20,433
Yes.

99
00:05:20,567 --> 00:05:22,133
Thank God, we're safe.

100
00:05:25,433 --> 00:05:26,567
For now.

101
00:05:41,333 --> 00:05:44,900
What the hell?

102
00:05:45,033 --> 00:05:47,467
Hey, compose yourself.

103
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,600
Sorry.

104
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,200
Sir!

105
00:05:56,333 --> 00:05:57,100
Yes?

106
00:05:57,233 --> 00:05:58,733
Good morning.

107
00:05:58,867 --> 00:06:00,967
Andrew Dizon, by the way.

108
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,300
What?

109
00:06:02,433 --> 00:06:06,200
Are you looking for trouble
with us in uniform again?

110
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:10,533
Sir, I'm just reporting
the truth.

111
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:15,200
Like now, I'm just here
to find out the truth.

112
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,567
Okay, okay.

113
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:20,067
Maybe you'll say something else,
so I'll tell you.

114
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,267
This is a gang war,

115
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:24,000
it's not the first time
this has happened in this area.

116
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:27,433
Or maybe you'll blame it
on the police again.

117
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:29,700
No, Sir.

118
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:31,967
Thank you, Sir.

119
00:06:34,667 --> 00:06:35,433
Is that it?

120
00:06:35,567 --> 00:06:37,033
Aren't we going to investigate?

121
00:06:39,533 --> 00:06:41,267
Well, let's go.

122
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:56,267
You lost control
of the situation, Lisa.

123
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:59,733
You even hurt yourself.

124
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:05,267
I had to spend money cleaning up
the mess you made last night.

125
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,833
It wasn't supposed to be
like that.

126
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:13,367
You know me.

127
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,633
I work clean.

128
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:20,833
But last night, there was an
unexpected complication.

129
00:07:21,967 --> 00:07:23,400
And that complication?

130
00:07:25,433 --> 00:07:27,733
Will that be a problem
for us again?

131
00:07:29,933 --> 00:07:31,433
I'll take care of Jin Ho.

132
00:07:31,567 --> 00:07:32,800
Don't worry.

133
00:07:34,167 --> 00:07:35,767
Make sure of it.

134
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,700
We already tied up one loose end
with Major Delgado.

135
00:07:40,833 --> 00:07:43,633
Don't start another problem.

136
00:07:43,767 --> 00:07:47,333
It's good that Parak fixed
the mess you made.

137
00:07:48,733 --> 00:07:52,100
We just made it look like
a gang war happened,

138
00:07:52,233 --> 00:07:54,900
so there weren't too many
questions.

139
00:07:55,033 --> 00:07:58,867
There's no need to complicate
things.

140
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,567
You're welcome.

141
00:08:03,033 --> 00:08:06,433
Did you ask your people
if they saw the flash drive?

142
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:09,933
No...

143
00:08:10,067 --> 00:08:12,333
No, why? What's in it?

144
00:08:12,467 --> 00:08:14,800
It contains a video
of me and Ramon

145
00:08:14,933 --> 00:08:16,933
that I need to recover.

146
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,167
What does that mean?

147
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:09,133
Can the flash drive
still be fixed?

148
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:11,733
Negative.

149
00:09:14,033 --> 00:09:16,267
Is it really impossible
to do something?

150
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:18,167
Why don't you try again?

151
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,033
Aren't I really impressed
with you

152
00:09:21,167 --> 00:09:22,633
because you're so good at that?

153
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,067
You're really fooling me,

154
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,800
but okay.

155
00:09:27,967 --> 00:09:30,133
I'll find a way to do this.

156
00:09:30,267 --> 00:09:33,200
I really need something else
to fix this.

157
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:34,367
Okay, Peter, okay,

158
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:35,900
let's find a way because that's
the only thing

159
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:37,700
that can really help Father.

160
00:09:41,067 --> 00:09:43,533
Don't worry. We'll find a way.

161
00:09:43,667 --> 00:09:45,467
I know how important this is
for you.

162
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,733
That's why so many other people
want it.

163
00:09:48,867 --> 00:09:51,400
Think about it. We almost died
because of this.

164
00:09:57,433 --> 00:09:59,867
Joey already has the flash
drive,

165
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,733
but...

166
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:03,333
But what?

167
00:10:03,467 --> 00:10:06,100
But there's someone else
after it.

168
00:10:07,633 --> 00:10:09,867
Joey almost got herself killed.

169
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,067
And even though we asked
for help,

170
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,100
the flash drive is still
not working.

171
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:18,567
But you know your daughter,

172
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:22,567
she'll find a way to fix
the flash drive.

173
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:24,933
I told her not to interfere.

174
00:10:25,067 --> 00:10:26,800
Well, she inherited that
from someone else.

175
00:10:26,933 --> 00:10:28,033
But...

176
00:10:29,167 --> 00:10:30,833
we have a bigger problem.

177
00:10:30,967 --> 00:10:33,200
I think the people we
encountered last night

178
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:35,733
have connections to the police.

179
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:37,733
You know, that's what I
suspected too.

180
00:10:39,333 --> 00:10:42,033
Ramon records all their
meetings,

181
00:10:42,167 --> 00:10:46,933
and there's a name that always
comes up Codename, Parak.

182
00:10:50,367 --> 00:10:51,500
Parak could be anyone.

183
00:11:02,533 --> 00:11:05,567
I think that Parak
has a position,

184
00:11:06,167 --> 00:11:07,600
whoever he is.

185
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:14,633
Do you have any other info
that might help us?

186
00:11:14,767 --> 00:11:17,100
You know, I'm still studying
the codes.

187
00:11:17,233 --> 00:11:20,667
The others, maybe timestamps,
but I'm still not sure.

188
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,100
I'll study them.

189
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:23,467
I'll let you know.

190
00:11:26,433 --> 00:11:30,067
Andrew, I have a favor
to ask of you.

191
00:11:31,567 --> 00:11:35,967
If you can, tell Joey not
to interfere.

192
00:11:38,333 --> 00:11:39,667
First of all,

193
00:11:41,767 --> 00:11:43,833
I'm here to help you.

194
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:49,567
Second, she doesn't trust me.
She won't listen to me.

195
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:54,733
Third, I'm not here to babysit
your daughter.

196
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,133
Is that software really 4k?

197
00:12:03,267 --> 00:12:05,967
You know,
this is the cheapest one.

198
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,800
Because recovery tools
are really more expensive.

199
00:12:08,933 --> 00:12:11,367
Worse, we're not sure
if it can be done.

200
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:15,533
This laptop is already old.

201
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:18,400
Do you need a new laptop?

202
00:12:18,533 --> 00:12:22,067
It doesn't have to be brand new.
All you need is high specs.

203
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:28,467
We've already had a hard time
getting you back,

204
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,500
and now you'll make us
spend more money.

205
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,600
Lord, help, please.

206
00:12:45,933 --> 00:12:47,100
Hello, Mother?

207
00:12:47,233 --> 00:12:48,567
Joey...

208
00:12:48,733 --> 00:12:50,800
Are you okay?

209
00:12:50,933 --> 00:12:52,733
<i> I'm okay.</i>

210
00:12:52,867 --> 00:12:55,100
I miss you so much.

211
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:57,733
<i>You know, it's so quiet here
at home.</i>

212
00:12:59,133 --> 00:13:01,667
What do you think, Joey?

213
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,900
I'm thinking about finding
a job first.

214
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,167
<i> Are you crying, Joey?</i>

215
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:10,733
What happened?

216
00:13:12,067 --> 00:13:13,600
I'm just frustrated.

217
00:13:13,733 --> 00:13:15,700
Frustrated? Why?

218
00:13:17,967 --> 00:13:20,800
I'm doing everything
I can to help Father.

219
00:13:20,933 --> 00:13:24,833
I just want him to be free
so we can be whole again.

220
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,067
Joey...

221
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:30,900
I understand what you're
feeling,

222
00:13:31,033 --> 00:13:32,700
what you're going through.

223
00:13:32,833 --> 00:13:36,933
But what you want to happen
is impossible.

224
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:42,100
So I hope you don't blame
yourself.

225
00:13:43,667 --> 00:13:44,733
Well, that's the thing.

226
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:48,700
I've found evidence to help
Father but it's broken.

227
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:51,033
It's not easy to fix.

228
00:13:53,233 --> 00:13:56,133
<i>Joey, don't solve the problem
alone.</i>

229
00:13:56,300 --> 00:14:00,067
You know, it's better
to call your Godfather Diego.

230
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:09,700
Yeah, that's it!

231
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,200
Yes?

232
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:24,533
You know, your mother was right.

233
00:14:25,633 --> 00:14:28,067
I think that's what you should
have done first.

234
00:14:29,567 --> 00:14:31,000
Why not?

235
00:14:32,333 --> 00:14:35,433
Didn't Father say not to tell
anyone?

236
00:14:35,567 --> 00:14:37,600
Maybe someone else would get
hurt.

237
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:42,467
Friendship! Boarders! Get out,
quickly! What's with you?

238
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:44,767
Hurry, I'll introduce you
to someone!

239
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:47,133
It seems like Lola's butt
is covered in ice.

240
00:14:47,267 --> 00:14:49,200
She's all giddy. Who is that?

241
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:51,833
Hurry up.

242
00:14:51,967 --> 00:14:54,067
- Wait, who is that?
- These guys are taking so long!

243
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,500
His name is...

244
00:14:57,633 --> 00:15:00,033
Jin Ho!

245
00:15:12,967 --> 00:15:14,067
You?

246
00:15:14,533 --> 00:15:15,600
What are you doing here?

247
00:15:15,733 --> 00:15:19,233
You know, I'm gonna stay here.

248
00:15:19,367 --> 00:15:20,967
You can't stay here!

249
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:21,900
Why?

250
00:15:22,033 --> 00:15:24,167
- Because...
- Who is that? Your ex?

251
00:15:27,133 --> 00:15:29,667
- Him? My ex?
- Is he your ex?

252
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,567
What ex? That's impossible,
Lola!

253
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:32,800
What are you saying?

254
00:15:32,933 --> 00:15:35,800
Why does it seem like there's
something?

255
00:15:35,967 --> 00:15:37,300
Is there something?

256
00:15:37,433 --> 00:15:40,867
Well, the three of us
are friends. Right?

257
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,167
We're friends, right?

258
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,467
Yeah.

259
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:44,767
Friends.

260
00:15:45,867 --> 00:15:48,733
My God, you guys are driving me
crazy.

261
00:15:48,867 --> 00:15:50,467
I was so nervous about you.

262
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:55,367
I thought I was going to have,
you know, a rival for my baby.

263
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,533
It's a good thing you said you
were friends.

264
00:15:57,667 --> 00:16:01,800
Because then,
he'll sleep in your room.

265
00:16:04,167 --> 00:16:06,233
What is this? It's annoying.

266
00:16:06,367 --> 00:16:09,267
Okay, you take care of this,
okay?

267
00:16:09,433 --> 00:16:10,900
Is he gonna show you the room,
okay?

268
00:16:11,033 --> 00:16:12,633
I'll see you later, okay?

269
00:16:13,967 --> 00:16:16,600
What's up, friend?
You called at the wrong time.

270
00:16:16,733 --> 00:16:18,867
What are you doing here?
Your place is better!

271
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:24,767
Because you're still in danger
and Theresa is still out there.

272
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:28,300
I'm here to protect you,
to be your bodyguard.

273
00:16:28,433 --> 00:16:31,133
For free?

274
00:16:31,267 --> 00:16:34,033
Even if it's free,
I don't need a bodyguard!

275
00:16:34,167 --> 00:16:36,833
I don't need you to protect me.
I know taekwondo.

276
00:16:36,967 --> 00:16:39,000
Yeah, that's automatic.

277
00:16:39,133 --> 00:16:41,100
But what if you're in trouble?

278
00:16:41,233 --> 00:16:43,633
At least we have someone
to call. Right, oppa?

279
00:16:45,867 --> 00:16:48,133
Are you talking to me?

280
00:16:48,267 --> 00:16:49,133
Yeah.

281
00:16:49,267 --> 00:16:51,333
That's what they call Korean
guys, right?

282
00:16:51,467 --> 00:16:52,500
Oppa!

283
00:16:52,633 --> 00:16:54,200
Yeah, but you know...

284
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:57,800
Okay, we can't do anything
if he wants to live here.

285
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:00,600
You can live here.
Just stay out of my way.

286
00:17:00,733 --> 00:17:01,600
Clear?

287
00:17:01,733 --> 00:17:02,900
Clear!

288
00:17:03,033 --> 00:17:07,133
You know, you won't even notice
me because I'm good at my job.

289
00:17:07,267 --> 00:17:08,600
Whatever.

290
00:17:12,133 --> 00:17:12,967
Come.

291
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:15,500
I'll show you to our room, Oppa.

292
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,233
The Congressman's people are
still picking up our supplies.

293
00:17:28,367 --> 00:17:30,333
They're on their way
to the factory.

294
00:17:30,467 --> 00:17:33,000
They've doubled their orders
now.

295
00:17:33,133 --> 00:17:37,067
I'll also make sure that their
route is clear

296
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:39,433
so that the police won't be
blocking them anymore.

297
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:41,700
Good.

298
00:17:42,933 --> 00:17:45,167
Our operations have been smooth
again

299
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:47,400
since that Delgado was locked
up.

300
00:17:47,533 --> 00:17:50,267
Maybe that policeman can
perform a miracle,

301
00:17:50,433 --> 00:17:52,733
and we'll have another problem.

302
00:17:52,867 --> 00:17:54,967
Why don't we just finish him
off?

303
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:56,200
Hey.

304
00:17:56,333 --> 00:17:58,200
Just chill.

305
00:17:58,333 --> 00:18:01,267
You, you're making your own
ghost.

306
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:04,467
Because I want to put a bullet
in that Delgado's head

307
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:08,100
so he can become a real ghost.

308
00:18:08,233 --> 00:18:09,800
That's Parak's strategy.

309
00:18:11,933 --> 00:18:14,067
I'm sure he's already cooking up
his plan.

310
00:18:18,233 --> 00:18:21,167
He knows what to do, right?

311
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:45,600
Hello, Joey?

312
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:49,933
Godfather, can we meet?
It's important.

313
00:18:50,067 --> 00:18:52,667
Sure. Why? What's that about?

314
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,133
It's about the evidence
I was talking about

315
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,533
that will help Father to be
free.

316
00:19:15,033 --> 00:19:16,133
Joey?

317
00:19:24,967 --> 00:19:26,100
Yes, Elai?

318
00:19:27,233 --> 00:19:29,567
I just want to remind you
about our recording.

319
00:19:29,733 --> 00:19:31,367
<i> We've set up here.</i>

320
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:34,500
Shocks. I'm sorry. I forgot.

321
00:19:34,633 --> 00:19:37,533
I'm just here at Joey's house.

322
00:19:37,667 --> 00:19:39,033
I just really have to talk
to her

323
00:19:39,167 --> 00:19:41,467
because I think she's up
to something bad.

324
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:43,100
I'll be back. I promise.

325
00:19:43,233 --> 00:19:44,800
Okay.

326
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:45,933
Bye.

327
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,767
Lord, I'm not that kind,

328
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:55,267
but why do my blessings seem to
be at their maximum right now?

329
00:19:56,667 --> 00:19:57,833
Yes?

330
00:19:59,033 --> 00:20:00,667
Is Joey there?

331
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:02,367
Is it possible to talk to her?

332
00:20:02,533 --> 00:20:04,133
What's that?

333
00:20:04,267 --> 00:20:07,100
Oh my, Joey is already gone,
she left already.

334
00:20:07,233 --> 00:20:10,467
Why would you look for someone
who isn't there?

335
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,933
I mean, I'm here.

336
00:20:28,267 --> 00:20:30,033
Will you please stop?

337
00:20:30,167 --> 00:20:32,167
Didn't I tell you
I'm going by myself?

338
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:34,667
I told you I'm your bodyguard.

339
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:38,033
I'm here to protect you
from any possible attacker.

340
00:20:39,767 --> 00:20:42,100
As for me, I'll watch over Oppa.

341
00:20:42,233 --> 00:20:44,900
Please. I'm going alone.

342
00:21:03,467 --> 00:21:04,267
Godfather...

343
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:12,800
- Godfather.
- My child.

344
00:21:12,933 --> 00:21:14,433
How are you?

345
00:21:14,567 --> 00:21:16,033
What evidence are you talking
about?

346
00:21:16,167 --> 00:21:17,367
What's that about?

347
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:20,233
The day Ramon Orbos died,

348
00:21:20,367 --> 00:21:24,333
I saw someone a woman and her
companions torturing him...

349
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:27,300
And then I took a video.

350
00:21:31,533 --> 00:21:32,667
Here it is.

351
00:21:39,367 --> 00:21:42,067
<i>Did you ask your people
if they saw a flash drive?</i>

352
00:21:42,233 --> 00:21:46,700
<i>It contains a video of me and
Ramon that I need to recover.</i>

353
00:21:47,667 --> 00:21:48,800
So this is it?

354
00:21:50,433 --> 00:21:51,600
Yes, Godfather.

355
00:22:01,133 --> 00:22:02,367
Please watch over my wife
and daughter.

356
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:04,233
Help me protect my family.

357
00:22:04,367 --> 00:22:06,167
You shouldn't trust anyone.

358
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:08,100
Your father wants to warn you

359
00:22:08,233 --> 00:22:10,300
because we don't know
who the real allies are.

360
00:22:10,433 --> 00:22:12,900
Me, I'm thinking while you guys
are moving impulsively.

361
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:16,767
Focus on Berdugo's orders,
that is, to kill Delgado.

362
00:22:16,933 --> 00:22:18,500
It's Diego...

363
00:22:18,633 --> 00:22:19,867
Impossible.
